# Cube bookshelf, top-down (issue 047): the divider seen from above and in front, like the other furniture: the light oak top with what sits on it (a sansevieria, a stack of books on a wooden tray, a white bowl, a stone vase of dried flowers) and the shelf's south end as the front slice. 1x4 tiles. The book and object detail of the old face-on drawing is kept as `view-bookshelf` (not drawn into the room).
size: 16x64
